<!--page {"title": "Motion Design for Startups: Showreels, Product Videos and UI Motion · Libre Studio", "description": "Motion design for startups: showreels, product explanation videos, app animations and UI micro-interactions, built on motion tokens so every movement feels like the same brand.", "path": "/motion-design/", "nav": "services"} -->
{{> head}}
{{> nav}}
<main id="main">

  <section class="section hero scheme-dark case-hero" aria-labelledby="md-title">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Motion design</p>
          <h1 class="h1" id="md-title" data-split>Motion design with a <span class="mark">job<svg class="mark__svg" viewBox="0 0 240 24" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-draw><path d="M4 15 C 46 8, 92 19, 136 12 S 210 7, 236 13"/></svg></span></h1>
          <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>Showreels, product videos, app animations and interface motion for startups. Every movement reveals, guides or emphasises something. Nothing moves just to move.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions actions--center" data-reveal>
          <a class="btn btn--lime" href="{{calendar}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="Book a Call">Book a Call</span></span></a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost-dark" href="/#reel"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="Watch our showreel">Watch our showreel</span></span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="make-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="make-title" data-split>What we make</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Showreels</strong> that show a studio or a product in under a minute and a half, cut for the website, LinkedIn, Instagram and Upwork.</li>
            <li><strong>Product explanation videos</strong> and walkthroughs that show how an app works, screen by screen.</li>
            <li><strong>App animations:</strong> splash screens, onboarding moments and loading states, delivered as video, Lottie or code.</li>
            <li><strong>Interface motion:</strong> page transitions, scroll reveals and micro-interactions, built in CSS or GSAP.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="rules-title" data-split>Motion as part of the system</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>Motion gets tokens, just like colour and type: a small set of durations and easing curves, named and reused everywhere. That is why a showreel, an app splash and a button hover from us feel like the same brand.</p>
          <p>Our own rules: ease-out entrances, short distances, hard-edged wipes instead of crossfades, nothing bouncy. And every animation has a reduced-motion version, so people who turn motion off still get everything, just without the movement.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-coral" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="container ai-def">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="tagline" data-reveal>Example</p>
        <h2 class="h2" id="example-title" data-split>The MONA AI splash</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
        <p>For <a class="text-link" href="/work/mona-ai/">MONA AI</a>, an AI photo and video app, golden shards drift in from a navy void and lock into place, one by one, until they form the MONA logo.</p>
        <p>We made the film with Kling AI, image-to-video from the real logo file, so the final frame is exactly the brand mark, with the movement directed in a written prompt. We also delivered the transformation as a React Native component, so the developers could drop it into the app instead of rebuilding it from a video.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="more-title">
    <div class="container ai-def">
      <h2 class="h2" id="more-title" data-split>More motion work</h2>
      <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our showreel.</strong> 84 seconds of studio work, with a silent 43-second loop at the <a class="text-link" href="/#reel">top of our homepage</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>The Echopod UX audit walkthrough</strong>, a full audit explained on video. <a class="text-link" href="https://youtu.be/a6h4D_BZkbM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch it on YouTube</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>The <a class="text-link" href="/work/tales-ai-landing/">Tales AI landing page</a></strong>, with GSAP scroll reveals and a night sky of drifting stars.</li>
          <li><strong>This website.</strong> Headlines that rise word by word, hand-drawn marks that draw on, a transit-map hiring line.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-royal" aria-labelledby="md-faq-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="md-faq-title" data-split>FAQs</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__list" data-reveal>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion open>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>How long is a showreel?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Usually 40 to 90 seconds, with shorter cuts for social and a silent loop for a website hero. Ours is 84 seconds, with a 43-second cut.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>Do you use AI video tools?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Yes, where they help, like Kling AI for the MONA splash. We direct them from real brand files and written prompts, and a designer approves every frame that ships.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>What formats do you deliver?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Video in every aspect ratio you need, Lottie for apps, and code (CSS, GSAP or React Native) for motion that lives inside a product.</p></div></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{> work-next-motion}}
</main>
{{> footer}}
